From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 5446 (D792): a solved goal is remembered on its helpers and
 finds them next time

Founder ruling D792 (16 Oct): the real TBC loan was unblocked by hand
(Tornike, Beso, Tiko) and Netai learned nothing from it. Netai must remember
such cases without asking the helper or telling anyone, and use them only
to suggest that person next time, with no reason given.

- Migration 246: helper_solved_cases, one row per helper per goal, holding
  the goal's own words.
- When a goal closes as finished, every helper whose ask was answered (not
  declined, not a no or later) is recorded, in the same hook that offers
  the helper thanks.
- search_by_tag's main search reads the record beside the member's own
  work: a match on the goal's words finds a helper the asker holds, ranks
  them as a structured hit, and carries self_work, so the model gets the
  approved BP note (offer them, never say why) and no new text.

The second-degree path (a helper only through one of the asker's contacts)
and the job-to-ties inference are not in this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
